1
00:05:54,545 --> 00:06:00,545
Every town has a story. Tombstone has a legend.

2
00:11:49,090 --> 00:11:55,090
Tombstone is a western, action film directed by George P. Cosmatos.

3
00:17:43,636 --> 00:17:49,636
Legendary marshal Wyatt Earp, now a weary gunfighter, joins his brothers Morgan and Virgil
to pursue their collective fortune in the thriving mining town of Tombstone.

4
00:23:38,181 --> 00:23:44,181
But Earp is forced to don a badge again and get help from his notorious pal Doc Holliday
when a gang of renegade brigands and rustlers begins terrorizing the town.

5
00:29:32,727 --> 00:29:38,727
Wyatt Earp, played by Kurt Russell.

6
00:35:27,272 --> 00:35:33,272
Doc Holliday, played by Val Kilmer.

7
00:41:21,818 --> 00:41:27,818
Johnny Ringo, played by Michael Biehn.

8
00:47:16,363 --> 00:47:22,363
Curly Bill, played by Powers Boothe.

9
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
Frank McLaury, played by Robert John Burke.

10
00:59:05,454 --> 00:59:11,454
Josephine, played by Dana Delany.

11
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Tombstone is a 1993 American Western film directed by George P.

12
01:10:54,545 --> 01:11:00,545
Cosmatos, written by Kevin Jarre (who was also the original director, but was replaced early in production), and starring Kurt Russell and Val Kilmer, with
Sam Elliott, Bill Paxton, Powers Boothe, Michael Biehn, Dana Delany and Charlton Heston in supporting roles, and narration by Robert Mitchum.

13
01:16:49,090 --> 01:16:55,090
The film is loosely based on real events that took place in the 1880s in
Southeast Arizona, including the Gunfight at the O.K.

14
01:22:43,636 --> 01:22:49,636
Corral and the Earp Vendetta Ride.

15
01:28:38,181 --> 01:28:44,181
It depicts several Western outlaws and lawmen, such as Wyatt Earp,
William Brocius, Johnny Ringo, and Doc Holliday.

16
01:34:32,727 --> 01:34:38,727
Tombstone was released by Hollywood Pictures in theatrical wide release in the
United States on December 25, 1993, grossing $73.2 million worldwide.

17
01:40:27,272 --> 01:40:33,272
The film was a financial success, and in the Western genre, it ranks
number 25 in the list of highest-grossing films since 1979.

18
01:46:21,818 --> 01:46:27,818
Critical reception was generally positive, with the story,
directing, and acting receiving praise.

19
01:52:16,363 --> 01:52:22,363
Particular praise went towards Val Kilmer's memorable
performance as the hard-drinking Doc Holliday.

20
01:58:10,909 --> 01:58:16,909
The film has become a cult classic since its release.

21
02:04:05,454 --> 02:04:11,454
The film explores themes of right and justice, saloon,
arizona, retirement, historical figure.
